name o3-09-two-fronts-1
timeout 700
time 1973-10-06T12:00:00Z

# CAMPAIGN O3, SORTIE 9 OF 10 - YOM KIPPUR 1973: GROUND ATTACK IN CONTESTED AIRSPACE.
# TWO AXES AT ONCE, UNDER THE OWN UMBRELLA. THIS FILE IS THE CHAIN HEAD: o3-10-october-six.fbm inherits
# its strike force and its umbrella.
# CONTROL: none - a chain step is never a controlled variant (O1's rule).
# Spec, anchor and sources: doc/campaigns/o3-yom-kippur-1973.md. Format: doc/missions/campaign.md.
#
# THE ANCHOR is the simultaneity itself: 6 October 1973 was ONE coordinated Egyptian and Syrian attack
# on two fronts 400 km apart [T4], and the whole Israeli problem that afternoon was that the defence had
# to be in two places. This file is that shape at squadron scale - two axes 22.2 km apart, one defending
# CAP of four in the middle, and nothing in the format that lets either side choose.
#
# THE SUBSTITUTION AND ITS DIRECTION (stated in every O3 file): the MiG-29 stands in for the MiG-17 /
# Su-7 / Su-20 / MiG-21 of 6 October 1973, whose own catalogue rows are ALPHA and may not answer a
# campaign question. It makes the ATTACKER materially STRONGER than history; a bad O3 result therefore
# says more than the record did, a good one says nothing. The Israeli CAP is the `f16` module (the real
# defenders flew F-4, Mirage and A-4), which makes BLUE stronger too. The umbrella is NOT substituted
# (`sa2`/`sa3`/`sa6` are the anchor's own designations), but three positions stand for >200 and the
# `sa2` is not even present here - o3-04 MEASURED that a S-75 cannot engage anything at O3's forced
# 300 m ingress altitude (its floor is 450 m [T4]), so carrying it into a 21-unit file would add an
# actor that provably decides nothing. That is a measured omission, not a convenience.
#
# `C15` IS THE SUBJECT AND IT IS NAMED BEFORE THE RESULT. There is no time-on-target, no deconfliction
# and no lead tasking in this tree, so "simultaneous" here means IDENTICAL SPAWN GEOMETRY and nothing
# else: all eight strikers are 6.02 km from their own aim point at t = 0, so all eight release within
# 0.1 s of each other. And there is no defensive DECISION either (`C6`: no live controller), so "the
# defender must choose an axis" is not a choice the defender makes - it is what four F-16s on
# `set task intercept` do with the picture their own radars build. Both halves are absences and both are
# priced here rather than asserted.
#
# THE ARENA (all coordinates [SET]). Suez sector, `--elev const`, 0 m datum, no terrain masking (C4).
#   NORTH AXIS   yxa..yxd at 30.89-30.92 N, each 6.02 km west of its own `target_soft` at 32.62000 E
#   SOUTH AXIS   yxe..yxh at 30.69-30.72 N, FOUR aircraft against TWO `target_hard` - a doubled weight
#                of effort, and it is aimed at exactly the target class o3-02 MEASURED as unreachable
#                (a FAB-500 needs 12.1 m against a hardened structure and this director delivers 66 m).
#                That is deliberate: a commander who does not know his store's limit would double up
#                where the store cannot work, and this file shows what that buys.
#   THE UMBRELLA yxnod P-18 at 30.80000 32.26000, yxsa3 S-125 at 30.84000 32.31000, yxsa6 2K12 at
#                30.80000 32.40000, all `emcon free`, node transmitting `wcs free` - o3-04's policy, so
#                the fratricide channel is OPEN and measured at scale.
#                AND THE GEOMETRY IS ASYMMETRIC BY ARITHMETIC: the 2K12's 24 km reach [T4] covers the
#                NORTH aim points at 23.3 km and falls 57 m short of the SOUTH ones at 24.06 km
#                [DERIVED]. One axis has a low-level layer and the other does not, and nobody chose that.
#   THE CAP      four F-16s at 5 000 m on the 33.05000 E line, two biased north and two south, 41-45 km
#                out at t = 0
# Scale: 1 deg lat = 111 132 m, 1 deg lon at 30.80 N = 95 619 m [DERIVED].
#
# WHY NO STRIKER AND NO F-16 DECLARES `survive`, AND IT IS THE ONLY WAY THIS FILE IS READABLE.
# `missions/FBMissionRunner` ends the whole run at the first DECIDING FAILURE as well as at the first
# flight-monitor K.O., and a violated `survive` is a deciding failure. At O3's 300 m a shot-down striker
# also reaches the ground within seconds. With eight strikers and four fighters, one `survive` line
# anywhere would delete the other twenty units' story at the first casualty. So attrition is read off
# `UNIT_RESULT` and `campaign ATTRITION` instead, and the metric this file reports is W3's - STRIKERS
# THAT REACHED RELEASE - not a loss ratio. The umbrella declares nothing at all for the same reason.
#
# THE ONE TACTICAL QUESTION: WITH THE DEFENCE FORCED TO SPLIT, DOES SPLITTING THE ATTACK PAY - AND DOES
# THE RUN STAY DETERMINISTIC AT THIS SCALE?
#
# MEASURED (2026-07-30, --elev const, campaign step 9, fingerprint d819e5c103397b30, exit 3):
#   21 units and 34 actors, 700.0 s of sim in 11.6 s of wall clock.
#   8 OF 8 STRIKERS REACHED RELEASE, all within 0.1 s of each other at t = 26.2:
#     NORTH, 6.02 km finals   yxa 62.64  yxb 62.24  yxc 61.85  yxd 61.46 m   (across +48.28 on all four)
#     SOUTH, 6.02 km finals   yxe 56.77  yxg 56.12 m                        (across +48.37)
#     SOUTH, 8.02 km line astern  yxf 69.20  yxh 69.67 m                    (across +66.35)
#     -> THE LINE-ASTERN AIRCRAFT DOES NOT INHERIT ITS LEADER'S ERROR, IT HAS ITS OWN, AND THE ONLY
#        DIFFERENCE IS 2 KM OF FINAL: +48.4 -> +66.4 m of cross-track, which interpolates exactly onto
#        o3-03's 6 km / 12 km ladder. That is the spec's dropped mission 3 answered inside this file.
#   4 OF 4 SOFT AIM POINTS DESTROYED (yx9t1..yx9t4, north axis, one bomb each).
#   0 OF 2 HARD AIM POINTS TOUCHED. Four bombs on two hardened structures produced FOUR arrivals and NOT
#     ONE `damage DAMAGE` line - the doubled weight of effort bought exactly nothing, which is o3-02's
#     number arriving as a tactical consequence rather than as a table.
#   THE UMBRELLA fired 7 rounds and ALL SEVEN WENT TO ITS OWN STRIKERS - and it SPLIT ACROSS THE AXES:
#     yxsa3 put all four V-601 on yxe (south) and yxsa6 all three 3M9 on yxh (south). Attributed by
#     comparing every `sms LAUNCH_SOLUTION ... tgtLat/tgtLon` against both aircraft's telemetry: 22-95 m
#     from the intended MiG-29 and 1.1-2.2 km from the next one. ZERO arrived; closest `stores MISS` 3.5 km.
#     THE NORTH AXIS WAS NEVER SHOT AT BY ITS OWN BELT AND THE SOUTH AXIS WAS SHOT AT SEVEN TIMES, and
#     the reason is geometry alone: the 2K12's 24 km reach covers the north aim points at 23.3 km and
#     falls 57 m short of the south ones, so it engaged the south axis on the EGRESS instead.
#   THE CAP SPLIT TOO, AND CORRECTLY: 8 AIM-120 released, one pair per axis (yx9b1/yx9b2 -> yxa/yxb north,
#     yx9b3/yx9b4 -> yxg south), then a second pair. FOUR ARRIVALS INSIDE THE 10 M FUZE - 4.41 and 4.54 m
#     on yxa, 4.03 m on yxg, 5.35 m on yxd - AND NOT ONE KILL. Every one of the four degraded systems and
#     left the aircraft combat-effective. ZERO AIRCRAFT LOST ON EITHER SIDE in 700 s.
#   -> SO SPLITTING PAYS, AND IT PAYS FOR A REASON THAT IS NOT DECEPTION: the CAP has no mechanism to
#      divide (`C15`/`C6`), so each pair collapses onto the axis nearer its own spawn line - which means
#      a two-axis attack is engaged at HALF DENSITY per axis with no decision made by anybody. The
#      unengaged half of the effort achieved nothing anyway, because it was sent against the target class
#      the store cannot kill.
#   -> AND THE HONEST WARNING ATTACHED TO THAT: THIS FILE'S OUTCOME AXIS IS NOT ORDERED BY ITS INPUTS.
#      Four rounds arrived inside their own fuze and killed nothing, which is O2's own rule 12 verbatim -
#      the deciding variable is the damage ZONE, so anybody reading "0 losses" as a property of the split
#      is reading a warhead's arrival geometry.
#
# READING RULE: exit 3 = TIMEOUT is the EXPECTED shape - four `kill unit` objectives on hardened
# structures can never be met and no unit declares `survive`, so nothing concludes and the clock runs
# out. THE MEASUREMENT is, in this order: (1) how many strikers reached release, with their `aimErrM`;
# (2) which aim points died, by class; (3) every `site LAUNCH` with the `sms LAUNCH_SOLUTION` above it,
# attributed to a callsign; (4) which axis the CAP engaged and how many AIM-120 arrived; (5)
# `UNIT_RESULT` for the attrition that the chain then carries into sortie 10 - which turned out to be
# NO LOSSES and eight `stores` entries, so the carry into 10 is eight aircraft with one FAB-500 each.
# exit 0 is impossible (the hard-target objectives cannot be met); exit 2 would be a defect.

zone umbrella 30.84000 32.31000 35000 100 18000
zone ceiling  30.80000 32.45000 90000 2200 20000

net crossing
  control yxnod
  link wire
  period 4.0
  hold 3
  wcs free
  member yxnod
  member yxsa3
  member yxsa6

# ---- NORTH AXIS: four aircraft, four artillery positions ----
unit yxa
  module mig29
  team hostile
  flight north 1
  spawn 30.89000 32.55700 300 90.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set n019_emission off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 fab500
  set store 6 fab500
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode opt
  wp 30.89000 32.62000 300 450
  wp 30.95000 32.30000 300 450
  objective kill unit yx9t1

